(1873937, 257302, 37529, '<td valign="top">Excellent camoflage shot.  Nice capture, focus is right on.</td>', 'Excellent camoflage shot.  Nice capture, focus is right on.', '2005-11-16 16:04:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1873939, 258003, 12448, '<td valign="top">Yes they do!  Great shot, nice capture overall.  As I''m sure you''ve heard or are going to hear, focus.  Nothing is in sharp focus and a soft focus doesn''t really work well with this shot for my personal taste.  I''m guessing it was a quick shot before the little guy took off and they are fast, this I know having had to catch them when working at a pet store.<br/> <br/>He blends in very well with the wall itself  an dif you could have captured him just on the wall that would have been great because the leaves are a bit distracting, especially the one in the front that is so bright.  But getting it just as he''s looking at the camera, WTG! :)  A 6</td>', 'Yes they do!  Great shot, nice capture overall.  As I''m sure you''ve heard or are going to hear, focus.  Nothing is in sharp focus and a soft focus doesn''t really work well with this shot for my personal taste.  I''m guessing it was a quick shot before the little guy took off and they are fast, this I know having had to catch them when working at a pet store. He blends in very well with the wall itself  an dif you could have captured him just on the wall that would have been great because the leaves are a bit distracting, especially the one in the front that is so bright.  But getting it just as he''s looking at the camera, WTG! :)  A 6', '2005-11-16 16:04:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1873960, 258166, 12448, '<td valign="top">This is a very nice shot, catching them all in flight was a very nice move.  I love watching them take off and land, it''s so pretty.<br/> <br/>The shot is very nice overall, though your main subject,the birds take up a very small space they still draw you in by the dark outlines of their bodies and the reflections on the water.  The one goose (I''m guessing they are geese) in the front middle seems pretty clear while every thing else is just a touch out of focus.  That is a neat trick, nice DOF for that.  My only complaint is the coloration of the sky, the yellow edge to the gray top, if you cuold have adjusted the levels or color balances or saturation to make it pop just a bit more this would probably have gotten a few extra points from me.  But as is, a 6</td>', 'This is a very nice shot, catching them all in flight was a very nice move.  I love watching them take off and land, it''s so pretty. The shot is very nice overall, though your main subject,the birds take up a very small space they still draw you in by the dark outlines of their bodies and the reflections on the water.  The one goose (I''m guessing they are geese) in the front middle seems pretty clear while every thing else is just a touch out of focus.  That is a neat trick, nice DOF for that.  My only complaint is the coloration of the sky, the yellow edge to the gray top, if you cuold have adjusted the levels or color balances or saturation to make it pop just a bit more this would probably have gotten a few extra points from me.  But as is, a 6', '2005-11-16 16:10:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1873963, 257733, 44882, '<td valign="top">took me at least two seconds to see her ! great idea.</td>', 'took me at least two seconds to see her ! great idea.', '2005-11-16 16:11:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1873965, 257640, 37529, '<td valign="top">Good job.  Had to look twice for the cute dog.  Fits right in.</td>', 'Good job.  Had to look twice for the cute dog.  Fits right in.', '2005-11-16 16:11:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1873973, 258197, 12448, '<td valign="top">Hey, I see you!  All tiny and quadrupled and wearing your red shirt or jacket! :)<br/> <br/>Nice idea, very unique in this is the first one I''ve seen like this.  I like the overall composition of the shot, the way ornaments line up, leading you in one side and out the other.  The DOF is well done also, bringing your focus in right at the first ornament and slowly fading out on either side.  It''s not tack sharp but it draws you to that focal point.  The shadows on the top are a bit distracting as is the upper left corner, keeps wanting to pull mu up there to that dark spot.  Color is nice, red is so hard to shoot as I am finding out, it can blow out rather quickly and really overpower a shot but you did very well on this one.  I''m giving this one an 8</td>', 'Hey, I see you!  All tiny and quadrupled and wearing your red shirt or jacket! :) Nice idea, very unique in this is the first one I''ve seen like this.  I like the overall composition of the shot, the way ornaments line up, leading you in one side and out the other.  The DOF is well done also, bringing your focus in right at the first ornament and slowly fading out on either side.  It''s not tack sharp but it draws you to that focal point.  The shadows on the top are a bit distracting as is the upper left corner, keeps wanting to pull mu up there to that dark spot.  Color is nice, red is so hard to shoot as I am finding out, it can blow out rather quickly and really overpower a shot but you did very well on this one.  I''m giving this one an 8', '2005-11-16 16:13:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1873983, 257872, 12448, '<td valign="top">Awwwwwww, so cute!  So patient and so understanding.  And I hope you gave them extra treats and belly rubs for doing this for you! :)<br/> <br/>Nice idea, not a bad concept at all.  I like the one dog closing their eyes and telling the other to do the same for the title, cute.  The light seems a bit harsh on the white dog and the crop seems very loose to me.  The whole bed area where it was taken on the top really isn''t needed to me.  If you crop it out it makes the viewer really concentrate on the dogs and their disguise. :)  A 5</td>', 'Awwwwwww, so cute!  So patient and so understanding.  And I hope you gave them extra treats and belly rubs for doing this for you! :) Nice idea, not a bad concept at all.  I like the one dog closing their eyes and telling the other to do the same for the title, cute.  The light seems a bit harsh on the white dog and the crop seems very loose to me.  The whole bed area where it was taken on the top really isn''t needed to me.  If you crop it out it makes the viewer really concentrate on the dogs and their disguise. :)  A 5', '2005-11-16 16:16:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1873990, 258245, 12448, '<td valign="top">Cooooooooooool!  I love this.  Saw it in the thumbnails and thought, this is gonna be good and I was right.<br/> <br/>First, congrats to you or your model for being so daring and thinking about this.  The lines on the wall work right into the lines on the model and blend very well.  The biggest problem I''m sure you will hear about is the light glare on the paint compared to the flat tone on the wall.  Being a basic challenge you couldn''t seperate them and make the adjustments that way.  Other than that, very well done, grand idea and you get a 9</td>', 'Cooooooooooool!  I love this.  Saw it in the thumbnails and thought, this is gonna be good and I was right. First, congrats to you or your model for being so daring and thinking about this.  The lines on the wall work right into the lines on the model and blend very well.  The biggest problem I''m sure you will hear about is the light glare on the paint compared to the flat tone on the wall.  Being a basic challenge you couldn''t seperate them and make the adjustments that way.  Other than that, very well done, grand idea and you get a 9', '2005-11-16 16:18:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1874001, 257203, 12448, '<td valign="top">Hey, you stole my cat! :)  Almost looks like my Tweety but she has white on her nose as wel.  Cute shot.  Good job getting the cat to look directly into the camera, I know exactly how hard that can be, LOL<br/> <br/>The idea is great, as I see a few other people had the same idea but the problems I see with this one is the cat''s not really camouflauged or disguises in any way.  An adjustment to levels and/or curves could have had the cat blending more into the background though the blue and black would never really match exactly.  If you had a black cloth or coat you could try this with.  Also an adjustment to color balance, to the yellow to make the eyes really come out and maybe another to contrast to really make them pop.  Normally this would get a 5 from me but because the subject is so darn cute, I''ll pop it up to a 6 :)</td>', 'Hey, you stole my cat! :)  Almost looks like my Tweety but she has white on her nose as wel.  Cute shot.  Good job getting the cat to look directly into the camera, I know exactly how hard that can be, LOL The idea is great, as I see a few other people had the same idea but the problems I see with this one is the cat''s not really camouflauged or disguises in any way.  An adjustment to levels and/or curves could have had the cat blending more into the background though the blue and black would never really match exactly.  If you had a black cloth or coat you could try this with.  Also an adjustment to color balance, to the yellow to make the eyes really come out and maybe another to contrast to really make them pop.  Normally this would get a 5 from me but because the subject is so darn cute, I''ll pop it up to a 6 :)', '2005-11-16 16:21:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1874005, 258234, 36988, '<td valign="top">Absolutely jaw dropping image... and the title kicks it into the highest gear. On my way out to buy my safari gear right away... Great job... :)<br/></td>', 'Absolutely jaw dropping image... and the title kicks it into the highest gear. On my way out to buy my safari gear right away... Great job... :)', '2005-11-16 16:24:05.000000', NULL, 1),
