(1902127, 257853, 7743, '<td valign="top">*** Critique Club ***<br/> <br/>First impressions: Nice subdued colours and fairly good placement of the main water droplet.  The image seems out of focus.<br/> <br/>Composition: <br/>What works:  -- The water droplet is placed at or near one of the points for rule of thirds.  -- The ripple to the left of the drop goes off on a diagonal which makes the image more dynamic<br/> <br/>What doesn''t work: The crop feels very tight all the way around.<br/> <br/>Exposure:<br/>For the most part the exposure seems right with only a few hot spots.<br/> <br/>Impact: Most of the impact seems to be achieved from the diagonal placement of the ripples.  I think the ripples could be placed more on the diagonal for more impact.  More impact would also be achieved if the image were sharper.<br/> <br/>Keep shooting.<br/> <br/>Colette<br/></td>', '*** Critique Club *** First impressions: Nice subdued colours and fairly good placement of the main water droplet.  The image seems out of focus. Composition: What works:  -- The water droplet is placed at or near one of the points for rule of thirds.  -- The ripple to the left of the drop goes off on a diagonal which makes the image more dynamic What doesn''t work: The crop feels very tight all the way around. Exposure:For the most part the exposure seems right with only a few hot spots. Impact: Most of the impact seems to be achieved from the diagonal placement of the ripples.  I think the ripples could be placed more on the diagonal for more impact.  More impact would also be achieved if the image were sharper. Keep shooting. Colette', '2005-11-28 12:26:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(1903074, 257658, 25218, '<td valign="top"><b>&lt;&lt; Critique Club &gt;&gt;</b> <br/> <br/><b>Initial Impression:</b> <br/>Nice macro. The colors are a little off-putting, but hey, it''s nature, and they''re nice and vivid.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>A centered composition works well for macro shots, and this is no exception. Perhaps a more square crop would be more pleasing with the round flower head, but that may just be nit-picking.<br/> <br/><b>Color/Tone:</b> <br/>Very vivid colors, even if it''s not the most pleasant combination in my eyes. Did you try this as a black &amp; white or duotone? There''s plenty of contrast in the photo, and I wonder the caterpillar would have been more camouflaged?<br/> <br/><b>Focus/Exposure:</b> <br/>The focus is dead-on, and the depth of field gives the photo an almost 3D quality.<br/> <br/><b>Title:</b> <br/>Servicable. It is what it is. Can''t find too much fault with it - I have nothing better to suggest.<br/> <br/><b>Meets the Challenge:</b> <br/>Yes, I think so. I think I can see what you were going for: the rust of the flower head matching the rust of the caterpillar. I do wonder if black and white would have made it meet the challenge more, though.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Technically an almost flawless photo. Aesthetically, not the greatest, but certainly not bad.</td>', '<< Critique Club >>  Initial Impression: Nice macro. The colors are a little off-putting, but hey, it''s nature, and they''re nice and vivid. Composition: A centered composition works well for macro shots, and this is no exception. Perhaps a more square crop would be more pleasing with the round flower head, but that may just be nit-picking. Color/Tone: Very vivid colors, even if it''s not the most pleasant combination in my eyes. Did you try this as a black & white or duotone? There''s plenty of contrast in the photo, and I wonder the caterpillar would have been more camouflaged? Focus/Exposure: The focus is dead-on, and the depth of field gives the photo an almost 3D quality. Title: Servicable. It is what it is. Can''t find too much fault with it - I have nothing better to suggest. Meets the Challenge: Yes, I think so. I think I can see what you were going for: the rust of the flower head matching the rust of the caterpillar. I do wonder if black and white would have made it meet the challenge more, though. Summary: Technically an almost flawless photo. Aesthetically, not the greatest, but certainly not bad.', '2005-11-28 18:58:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1903080, 257959, 34659, '<td valign="top">One of the most amazing shots I''ve seen...  Spectacular job!  Congrats!</td>', 'One of the most amazing shots I''ve seen...  Spectacular job!  Congrats!', '2005-11-28 19:00:30.000000', NULL, 0),
